# A private field is a slot like any other. The class is evaluated once and has no private method, so nothing has to tell its objects from those of another evaluation: the instance has no word for that, and the class token is not read.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="make" role=ResultWrapper
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK: Double b@[[count]] = Patchpoint({{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[counter]] = Patchpoint($1(b@{{*}}):Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), {{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NEXT: Store(b@[[count]], b@[[counter]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK: Return(b@[[counter]], Terminal)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# CHECK-LABEL: name="make" role=ResultWorker
# CHECK-NOT: :GetModuleVariable
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# Nothing adds the private name by a call or has a write barrier.
# NONE-LABEL: name="make" role=ResultWrapper
# NONE-NOT: :PrivateSet
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSCell
# NONE-NOT: Reads:ObjectFields
# NONE-COUNT-2: Patchpoint(
# NONE-NOT: Patchpoint(
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
